mode: "100644"
text: "# Workflows, checklists & worked examples\n\n## The weekly episode → shorts loop\nTrim the source (pre-show/dead air out — credits bill on source minutes) → upload with genre + length + negative\nprompts set → candidates return scored → triage sort → human three-question pass (stands alone? fair? serves?) →\nedit top 3-5 / approve clean mid-scorers / discard ~40% without guilt → brand template across the batch →\ncaptions accuracy pass → export + download promptly → drip-schedule → WoopSocial → weekly: real retention vs\nscores, recalibrate.\n\n## The per-clip QA checklist (before anything publishes)\nHook's first line lands ✓ · caption errors fixed (names/jargon) ✓ · reframe drift checked (subject in frame) ✓ ·\nboundaries clean (no mid-word starts) ✓ · context fair to anyone quoted ✓ · brand template applied ✓ · music =\nlicensed or added natively at publish (auto-music off) ✓ · right aspect ratio per destination ✓.\n\n## The credit-math worksheet (before subscribing)\nMonthly source minutes = episodes × avg length (trimmed). Add +1/post if direct-posting to X. Compare to tier\nminutes (≈ Free 60 / Starter 150 / Pro 300 — verify in-app). A weekly 60-min show ≈ 240 min/mo → Starter won't\ncover it; Pro annual (~$14.50/mo) is the documented value pick. Editor gating conflicts across sources — confirm\nin-app before paying.\n\n## Score recalibration (monthly)\nLog each published clip: its score vs its real 3s-hold/watch-through. After ~20 clips you'll know how predictive\nthe score is for YOUR content — most creators find it useful for ranking, unreliable as prophecy. Adjust how much\ntriage weight it gets; never let it auto-decide.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (the triage discipline)\n\"60-minute episode. opus gave me 11 clips. old me would've edited all 11. new me: sorted by score, edited the top\n4, approved 3 clean mid-scorers untouched, binned 4 — including a 91 that made my guest sound like he was\nendorsing something he spent ten minutes criticizing. the score doesn't know context. i do.\" — triage not truth,\nthe fairness catch, ~40% binned.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the drip)\n\"One webinar became nine little clips — we didn't post them all at once. Two a week, each one read through first\n(the captions spelled a client's name three different ways, bless them), our template on every one, and the music\nswapped for a licensed track. Six weeks of gentle presence from one afternoon's recording. One small step: before\nyour next upload, trim the housekeeping off the front — the meter runs on what goes in, not what comes out.\" —\nQA pass, drip cadence, the credit tip.\n\n## Never\nAuto-post unreviewed clips · treat the score as a guarantee or auto-delete threshold · ship a clip that\nmisrepresents a speaker · skip the caption accuracy pass · feed burned-in-subtitle video · leave auto-music on\nfor commercial posts without checking rights · process untrimmed sources · assume the editor/API is on your tier\nwithout checking · leave exports undownloaded near renewal · claim WoopSocial clips video.\n"
